  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Minn. Stat. 624.7141, subd. 1): A person is guilty of a felony and may be sentenced to imprisonment for up to two years and to payment of a fine of not more than $10,000 if the person intentionally transfers a pistol or semiautomatic military-style assault weapon to another and the person knows that the transferee:\nSection 1 (Minn. Stat. 624.7141, subd. 2): A person who violates this section may be sentenced to imprisonment for up to five years and to payment of a fine of not more than $20,000 if the transferee possesses or uses the weapon within one year after the transfer in furtherance of a felony crime of violence."
